+## Unused border corrections
+
+Specialize unused sampler border corrections away ([mechanism](../../../docs/reference/rendering.md#unused-border-corrections-retain-sample-registers)). No sampler of this game needs a twin (no "border colour … Metal lacks" line, the mask 0 in every draw of a profiled frame), so every draw takes the specialization and the picture does not change. Measured on a MacBook Air M4, docked at render scale 0.75 (1920×1080), whole GPU, a window, in the fixed view of Hyrule Field with the most grass (`still.sh`), with the 264 render-stage shaders of that scene that sample through the corrections rebuilt in the new form beside the chain `971e0669b443` image and a host of that chain:
+
+- In-process A/B (`DM_AB DM_NVN_BORDER_KEEP=ab`, the same process, scene and temperature): GPU per frame 25.20 ms specialized against 26.69 and 26.79 ms with the corrections, about 1.5 ms, in the render stages; with the kernels too, a mean of 24.73 ms over five phases against 26.54 ms over four, 1.8 ms.
+- Separate runs, interleaved: 26.48 and 27.10 ms with the corrections, 26.00 and 25.46 ms specialized (thermal drift between runs is about 0.6 ms).
+- The earlier test-only experiment, every twin sample removed from all 301 shaders including 37 kernels, gave 24.97 ms against a four-run mean of 26.36 ms.
+
+The prewarm built the 551 specialized bases of that scene in 11 s at the start, on background threads, before the measured frames. The offline archive of a full conversion holds them (`pso_offline.py`): a test archive of 24 scene pairs, 20 of them with a specialized pixel function, served all 24 to the host's descriptors.
+
+Its 37 kernels that correct samples, NDSR's network among them, gave about 0.25 ms more (GPU per frame 25.09 and 25.24 ms with their corrections, 24.97 and 24.86 ms without, interleaved runs; their compute encoders 0.3 ms faster in the profiled frames). Chain `da29694f3f98` contains the change for every stage; a full shader conversion with it is pending, and so is the target of at least 55 fps at these settings.
+
